data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** The syntax is straightforward:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[4];
```

This works in safe code (no `unsafe` needed) because assigning `stackalloc` directly to a `Span<T>` has been allowed since C# 7.2. On this 64-bit system, each `nint`/`nuint` is 8 bytes. The only quirk is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an unsafe context — use `nint.Size` instead if you need the size in safe code.
